  "notes": "Self-produced soul-sample rap sitting between the 90s lane and a modern low end, and the low end is where this entry differs from its neighbours. The research says \"808 sub with short glides on the modern cuts, sample bass on the traditional ones; sub sits under a mid-register loop\". ⚠ The boom-bap archetype nulls `drums.bass808` on purpose — it is a sampled kit and a break — so the 808 is modelled in `bassline` instead: `mirror_kick` at `followRootsProb` 0.9 with `glideProb` 0.25, the highest glide on this axis. That is an engine reading, not a claim that he programs an 808 lane. The chopped-soul topline is `melody.timbreHint` `vocal_chop` with `octaveJumpProb` 0.13 for pitched-up chops, and the harmony is the two families the research names — i–iv and i–VI–III–VII — with sevenths and triads near even. Hats are 8ths with 16th accents (`fillDensity` 0.42), and the claps that \"sometimes replace snares entirely\" are `rimshotLayer` false with the `snap` perc lane rather than a snare change. `switchUpProb` 0.3 is the documented third-act beat switch. ⚠ `session.halfTime` stays false. The research says \"some cuts read half-time with the backbeat on 3\", but flipping the flag moves the backbeat on every seed and this catalogue is overwhelmingly 2-and-4; that is an **unmodelled** claim rather than an inferred one. ⚠ `confidence` is medium — the research rates it medium-high at album level. The **INFERRED** numbers are `glideProb`, `fillDensity` and the ghost placement.",
